  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n\u00ac(A\u2227B)=\u00acA\u2228\u00acB\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(5>3\\text{\u00a0and\u00a0}7\\text{\u00a0is even}) & \u2261\u00ac((5>3)\u2227(7\\text{\u00a0is even})) \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac(5>3)\u2228\u00ac(7\\text{\u00a0is even}) \\\\  & \u2261(5\\le 3)\u2228(7\\text{\u00a0is odd}) \\\\  & \u22615\\le 3\\text{\u00a0or\u00a0}7\\text{\u00a0is odd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
